.TH IAXPHONE-GUI 1 "November 2026" "iaxphone 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
iaxphone\-gui \- IAX2 softphone window
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B iaxphone\-gui
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B iaxphone\-gui
is the window of
.BR iaxphone (1):
it registers with the IAX2 server, shows the registration and the current
call, and offers a number entry, a keypad, Call, Answer, Hang up and
Transfer buttons, Mute and Hold boxes and peak level meters.
.PP
The keypad dials when idle and sends DTMF during a call; a key sounds for
as long as it is held, 100 ms at least, and so is the DTMF held on the
wire. Incoming calls ring on the speaker and show a desktop notification.
Hold stops the audio both ways and lets the server play music to the
other party; Transfer sends the other party to the number in the entry (a
blind transfer), after which the server hangs up on us.
.PP
The gear button opens the settings: server, account, caller id,
registration, jitter buffer depth, preferred codec (Opus, G.711 \(*m-law or
A-law; the others stay accepted), sound (default devices or none), and
the microphone and speaker to use. They are stored in Fyne's preferences
under
.IR ~/.config/fyne/com.github.ppomes.iaxphone/ ,
the secret included, in clear.
.PP
The clock button opens the call history, newest first, missed calls
marked and the talk time shown; tapping an entry puts its number back in
the entry to call it. The history is one JSON line per call in
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/iaxphone/history.jsonl
.RI ( ~/.local/share
by default), kept to the last 500 calls.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/fyne/com.github.ppomes.iaxphone/preferences.json
The settings.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/iaxphone/history.jsonl
The call history.
.PP
On a desktop with a status area (StatusNotifierItem: GNOME with the
AppIndicator extension, KDE, Xfce...) a handset icon shows the state, grey
when not connected, blue when ready, orange while ringing, green in a
call. There the phone starts behind its icon, with no window, and closing
the window puts it back there while the phone keeps taking calls; the
icon, its menu (show, answer, hang up, quit) and an incoming call bring
the window up.
.PP
Only one
.B iaxphone\-gui
runs per user: starting a second one, from the applications menu say,
shows the window of the first and exits. They meet on a socket in
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR iaxphone (1)
